  "caption": "Quinn dusted off the old gym bag after two winters off. Week one felt amazing. By week four, knees and shins were complaining.\n\nFitness tends to come back faster than tendons, bone and cartilage adapt, so the body can feel ready before it really is. That is why aches often show up around week four.\n\nWhat can help: start at about half what you think you can do, add roughly 10% a week, do two short strength sessions weekly, and keep sessions regular rather than in big bursts. Treat a lingering niggle as a sign to ease back a little.\n\nGet checked (and see your GP) if you have chest symptoms, dizziness, breathlessness, or tiredness way out of proportion to the effort.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
